+### Assigned and assignees
+
+New issues default to unassigned in Backlog. Assigned requires at least one live GitHub assignee. Use `/task assign #N` to add the configured assignee (falling back to `@me`) and couple Backlog to Assigned through a locked, compensated invocation saga. GitHub does not provide one transaction across assignee and Projects Status writes, so the saga verifies each postcondition and compensates only the mutation it introduced. A nonzero mover exit triggers strict configured-project Status and assignee re-reads: if the target Status landed, the assignee change is preserved and the incomplete move remains nonzero; if the outcome cannot be proved, no destructive compensation runs. Compensation itself is successful only after a bounded, case-insensitive assignee postcondition read. Use `/task assign #N --assignee <login> --remove` to remove a login; removing the final assignee demotes only an issue currently in Assigned to Backlog. Refine through Done are assignment-neutral and never move backward when an assignee is removed. For a defect spawned mid-task, ask `[Y|n]` (default Yes) whether to self-assign; Yes creates with `--assignee @me`, No keeps the default.
